{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Behold, I am doing</b> — כלה [destruction]. Rabbi Moses said: like ושם עשו דדי בתוליהן (Ezekiel 23:8, 'there they pressed the breasts of their virginity'). And they are two conjugations, kal and heavy [piel]." "<b>And the meaning of 'in all the earth [for] their shame'</b> — the nations will be ashamed when they see the lame one who had become a praise. And Rabbi Moses said: like ונשלמה פרים שפתינו, האתן בכורי פשעי (Hosea 14:3), and likewise בכל הארץ [is] in place of בשתם."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites the two vocalizations of עֹשֶׂה (kal) and עֹשֵׂה (piel/heavy) as possible readings."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:36.082841003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}